---
/**
 * Problem-framing section. One tight paragraph about why context
 * dies between sessions, with a link to the full argument in docs.
 */
---

<section class="section">
	<div class="container">
		<h2 class="section-title">Why context keeps dying</h2>
		<p class="section-lede">
			Every AI coding session starts cold. You re-explain the same
			architectural decisions, the same licensing rules, the same
			reasons you picked SQLite over Postgres. The model burns most
			of its context window re-learning what you already told it
			yesterday, and by afternoon it's still confidently wrong about
			basic facts.
		</p>
		<p class="fix">
			CtxOne fixes this by giving your AI tools a real memory layer —
			stored locally, versioned like git, attributable like
			<code>git blame</code>, and cheap to query because it returns
			only the facts relevant to <em>this</em> question.
		</p>
		<p class="read-more">
			<a href="/why-ctxone/context-anxiety/">
				Read the full argument →
			</a>
		</p>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	.fix {
		color: var(--ctx-text);
		font-size: 1rem;
		max-width: 40rem;
		margin: 0 0 1.25rem 0;
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.fix code {
		background: var(--ctx-panel);
		border: 1px solid var(--ctx-border);
		padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
		border-radius: var(--ctx-radius-sm);
		font-size: 0.9em;
		color: var(--ctx-accent-text);
	}

	.fix em {
		color: #ffffff;
		font-style: italic;
	}

	.read-more {
		margin: 0;
		font-size: 0.9rem;
	}
</style>
